WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.360
This Aquaman actor had better get his hands
on a shiny leather jacket and a latex jumpsuit

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.460
he's going to need 'em for The Matrix 4.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.620
The announcement of a new addition to the
Matrix franchise, directed and co-written

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:17.260
by series originator Lana Wachowski, essentially
blindsided the film world in August 2019.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.760
Even more exciting than the confirmation that
Wachowski was set to helm The Matrix 4 was

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:26.319
news that original stars Carrie-Ann Moss and
Keanu Reeves would return to their iconic

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.800
roles as Trinity and Neo.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.020
Little news regarding The Matrix 4 came out
in the time since those announcements, but

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:37.050
now, it appears a new-to-the-franchise face
will join Moss' Trinity and Reeves' Neo in

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.300
their fight against the Matrix.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:44.140
That face belongs to Aquaman star Yahya Abdul-Mateen,
who played the villainous David Kane — better

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.640
known as Black Manta — in the Jason Momoa-led
superhero flick.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.380
"Call me…

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.620
Black Manta!"

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.800
Variety was the first to break the news that
Abdul-Mateen is circling a role in The Matrix

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.300
4.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.560
If the outlet's reporting proves accurate,
Abdul-Mateen's role won't merely be as a supporting

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.240
player to his iconic co-stars.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.620
Wachowski and The Matrix 4 producers have
reportedly spent some time in recent weeks

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:15.060
meeting with several actors over what's being
called a "secret role" in the upcoming film.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:19.400
While the exact nature of the character remains
a secret, we know that it's being referred

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.909
to as a lead role, and that Abdul-Mateen has
emerged from the recent casting talks as the

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:25.360
frontrunner to land the part.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:29.740
Though it's unclear who Abdul-Mateen will
play in the The Matrix 4, news of his potential

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.930
casting in the film should be met with cheers
from fans of the Matrix franchise and of the

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:38.520
actor himself, who has become one of the brightest
young stars in Hollywood in recent years.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.260
Abdul-Mateen is likely best known for his
turn as Manta in last year's unexpected blockbuster

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:49.280
Aquaman, but he's also delivered more-than-memorable
performances on Baz Luhrmann's musical series

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.090
The Get Down, in the Hugh Jackman-led circus
musical The Greatest Showman, and on Hulu's

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.120
breakout series The Handmaid's Tale.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:59.260
"So, are you brave, or… stupid?"

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.980
"I'm not brave, so… there you go."

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.940
Recently, Abdul-Mateen appeared in Jordan'
Peele's bone-chilling horror confection Us,

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.590
and on the "Striking Vipers" episode of Black
Mirror season 5.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:19.440
He'll next be seen on HBO's Watchmen series,
in Peele's Candyman remake, and as Black Panther

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.840
Party co-founder Bobby Seale in Aaron Sorkin's
The Trial of the Chicago 7.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:29.000
So yeah, if you're not overly familiar with
Yahya Abdul-Mateen's face, you can rest assured

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.410
that he'll be bringing some serious cred to
whatever role he plays in Wachowski's new

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:33.180
Matrix film.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.950
Unfortunately, it will probably be quite some
time before we find out who Abdul-Mateen will

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.500
play in The Matrix 4, as Wachowski and the
Warner Bros. team will likely want to keep

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.760
a very tight lid on plot and character details
which means we really have no idea what's

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:51.510
in store for The Matrix 4, and even less of
a clue how Abdul-Mateen's character will factor

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:52.140
into the action.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.580
Still, it will be interesting to see what
Wachowski does with the new film the first

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.020
movie she's directing without the help of
sister Lilly.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:03.620
Wachowski has enlisted a little help from
her friends in crafting The Matrix 4's secretive

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.120
narrative.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:09.720
Those friends include Cloud Atlas author David
Mitchell and screenwriter Aleksander Hemon,

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.340
both of whom contributed work to the Wachowskis'
beloved Netflix series Sense 8.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:19.590
While we know virtually nothing about what
the trio has done with The Matrix 4's script,

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:23.590
Reeves recently told Entertainment Tonight
that the story is, quote, "very ambitious,

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.340
as it should be."

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.920
That tease should be more than enough to get
any Matrix fan hyped about what's ahead for

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:33.900
Trinity and Neo and now Abdul-Mateen's mystery
character even if we do have a couple of years

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.980
before we find out what will happen in the
film.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:40.880
The Matrix 4 is scheduled to go before cameras
in 2020, with an undisclosed release date

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.920
slated for sometime in 2022.

